[ ] Project recurring occurrences into the action surfaces =occurrence-surface $Client-surface follow-on to VTODO sync: the action list becomes a windowed union of materialized actions + projected occurrences (render(master+deviations, window)). Occurrences have no .actions line. Seam: operations uniform, text-editing not. See README 'Client-surface projection (2026-07-24)'.$ !2 #019f962c-ba5a-7732-ad24-df6fceadea53
    >[ ] Verify the occurrence UUIDv5 canonicalizes the recurrence-id $Invariant. Normalize the recurrence key to the master DTSTART value-type/TZID BEFORE hashing into the UUIDv5, so peers emitting the same slot as UTC vs TZID-local vs floating derive the identical occurrence handle. Hash the immutable slot, never the occurrence's mutable DUE, or reschedules mint a new identity. Guards against ghost/duplicate occurrences. May already hold — verify against expand/identity code.$ !1 #019f962c-eb39-7312-9da0-b36b3a9bda90
    >[ ] Ingest a foreign roll-forward as occurrence completion $Invariant. A camp-B client (Apple Reminders etc.) completes a recurring VTODO by advancing the master DTSTART with no override. Import must recognize 'master advanced one period, no new override' as completion of the prior occurrence and record that deviation, not reinterpret it as a series reschedule. Verify the 3-way reconcile covers the recurring-master case.$ !1 #019f962c-eb46-77b3-931e-1e43920e7daa
    >[ ] Render the windowed union of actions and projected occurrences in the views =occurrence-view $unscheduled/agenda surface materialized actions AND projected occurrences together; each occurrence addressable by its occurrence UUIDv5. Window reuses the existing configurable defaults. No consumer branches on materialized-vs-projected.$ !2 #019f962c-eb51-72a3-9ab9-73b93dad5959
    >[ ] Route occurrence operations to deviations, not line edits =occurrence-ops $complete/reschedule/skip on a projected occurrence writes a RECURRENCE-ID override (or EXDATE) into the single Plan resource; the CLI resolves the occurrence handle. Materialized-action edits unchanged. This is the operations-uniform / text-editing-not seam made real on the write path.$ !2 <occurrence-view #019f962d-1f07-7091-a4af-9868afc2a1aa
    >[ ] Surface occurrences in nvim as virtual lines and code-actions $Keep the buffer honest: occurrences render as virtual lines/extmarks, never editable buffer text with nowhere to save back. Expose complete/reschedule/skip as LSP code-actions that invoke the occurrence-ops write path. org-agenda two-surface model: raw-file editing unchanged for materialized actions.$ !3 <occurrence-ops #019f962d-1f15-7c23-82d5-e1c8f2a652e0
